# CLI

The `permdock` binary follows the contract better-supabase's CLI defines, CLI contract 3 since better-supabase 0.58 (`docs/decisions/0037-cli-contract-shared-with-better-supabase.md`, `docs/decisions/0068-cli-contract-3.md`). Keep the names below identical in both repositories.

## Layout

- `src/cli/core/` holds the contract: `run`, `command`, `manifest`, `help`, `output`, `errors`, `io`, `agent`, `consent`, `completion`, `files`, `http`, `credentials`. `src/cli/project/` discovers the config, package manager and framework.
- `core/manifest.ts` is static data and the only list of commands: name, group, summary, examples, docs page, `effects`, `config`, `findings`. It imports no command module; each leaf has a `load()` with a dynamic import, so `--help` and `--version` load none.
- A command module in `commands/` declares its flags and positionals once, with a `description` for help. `run(argv, { cwd, io })` takes its environment, streams and `fetch` from `io`, so a test runs it without process globals.

## Contract

- **Exit codes**: `0` success, `1` failure or drift, `2` usage or action required (`userActionRequired`), `130` SIGINT or a cancelled prompt, `143` SIGTERM. There is no exit `3`. Throw a `CliError` with a kind; never `process.exit`.
- **Output**: stdout carries data only, stderr everything else. `--json` prints `cli-result-v2`: the result document (`status`, `data`, `warnings`, `next`) on stdout for a success or a report that exits 1, else one error document line on stderr (`status`, `reason`, `message`, `type`, `next`, `data`, `userActionRequired`, `retryable`). A `next` step has `command`, `argv` and `when`. `--help --json` prints `cli-commands-v1`. A change to either shape updates `schemas/`, `packages/permdock/tests/cli/cli-schemas.test.ts` and `packages/permdock/tests/better-supabase/cli-contract.test.ts`, which validates against better-supabase's own `cli-result-v2.json`.
- **`reason`**: snake_case, from `ProblemCode` in `core/errors.ts`, which gives each its exit code. Every reason is one of better-supabase's contract 3 reasons with its meaning and exit (`usage`, `unknown_command`, `config_invalid`, `file_conflict`, `input_required`, `confirmation_required`, `internal` and the rest); PermDock adds none. `CliError` `extensions` become the error document's `data`. `type` is `https://permdock.com/docs/cli/errors#<reason>`, and `apps/docs/content/docs/cli/errors.mdx` has one heading per reason. A plain `Error` is `internal` (exit 1) unless its message starts with `PermDock`, the library's prefix for a definition it rejects (`config_invalid`, exit 2); a config check in the CLI throws `configError()`.
- **Effects**: `files`, `rewrite`, `database:read`, `database:write`, `network`, `cloud:write`, `install`. A leaf lists every effect it may have; help prints them, and consent reads them.
- **Writing files** goes through the `FilePlan` in `core/files.ts`: `--dry-run`, `--check`, `--force`, all or nothing. A `rewrite` refuses files with uncommitted changes unless `--force`.
- **Agent mode** (`--agent`, `PERMDOCK_AGENT`, `detectAgent`): JSON by default, no prompts. Missing input returns `input_required` with `data.missing` and `next`. `rewrite`, `cloud:write` and `--force` over files return `confirmation_required` with `data.digest` and `data.effects` until the run passes `--yes --effects-digest <digest>`; `--yes` alone never stands in. A leaf whose stdout is a script for the shell sets `shellOutput`.
- **Secrets** never sit in argv: they come from a `--<name>-stdin` flag (`--db-url-stdin`, `--key-stdin`, `--token-stdin`) or an environment variable, and are redacted from every output. No flag takes a secret as its value.
- **Completion**: candidates come from the manifest. A flag or positional with a fixed set of values that is not an `enum` gets a `complete` hook, lazy when it needs a heavy module.

## Flag vocabulary

`--out <file>` (`-` for stdout) and `--out-dir <dir>`; `--format` picks the renderer (`text`, `json`, `github`, `sarif`) and `--kind` the document; `--only` and `--ignore` narrow what runs; `--force` only overwrites; `--fail-on` sets the severity threshold; `--check` and `--dry-run` come from the `FilePlan`; `--db-url`; `--policy` and `--permissions` name modules. A new flag reuses one of these before it adds a word.

## Renames

A renamed flag or moved command gets a row in `core/renames.ts`, which feeds the `flag_renamed` and `command_moved` hints and the `permdock codemod` CLI-call rewrite, plus the CLI table under "Renamed in" on `getting-started/naming.mdx`. `pnpm docs:drift` checks that they agree.

## Tests

- `tests/cli/__snapshots__/help/<leaf>.txt` snapshots every leaf's help; `packages/permdock/tests/cli/docs-flags.test.ts` checks each page lists its flags, no flag its commands do not take, and the `effects` of each command in its `Side effects` table.
- `packages/permdock/tests/cli/completion.test.ts` snapshots the scripts and checks the candidates.
- `scripts/cli-startup.ts` holds the startup budget, and `packages/permdock/tests/cli/startup-imports.test.ts` fails when `--help` or `--version` reaches a command module.
